question:
The reaction between nitrogen monoxide (NO) and bromine (Br₂) to form nitrosyl bromide (NOBr) is studied at a constant temperature. The initial rates of the reaction are measured for different initial concentrations of NO and Br₂, leading to the following data points: 

[NO]₀ = 0.1 M, [Br₂]₀ = 0.2 M → Initial rate = 4 × 10⁻⁴ M/s; 
[NO]₀ = 0.2 M, [Br₂]₀ = 0.2 M → Initial rate = 8 × 10⁻⁴ M/s; 
[NO]₀ = 0.2 M, [Br₂]₀ = 0.4 M → Initial rate = 3.2 × 10⁻³ M/s.

Based on this data, what is the overall order of the reaction?
